On June 8, 2015 at 2:17:36 AM, Gleki Arxokuna (gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com) =
wrote:

yet another post in English (feel free to find words for


=C2=A0"syntactic tree",
lu jufra stura li'u ja lu jufra seljimca li'u

=C2=A0"node",
tcana

"level in the syntactic tree",
yyy senta befi lo jufra seljimca

=C2=A0"reset"
refcfa

=C2=A0and "refer to one level up").
krasi fa lo li'erla'i senta befi lo jufra seljimca



Several tools are currently used for moving to other levels of the tree:
1. no'a - shifts one level down
2. lo - shifts one level up
3. ku - shifts one level down
4. vo'a - temporarily resets to level 0 (proposed =3D {no'axiro})
5. {xoi} (proposed meaning) - temporarily shifts one level up
6. {soi} (proposed meaning) - temporarily resets to level 0
7. {i} - explicitly marks level 0
8. {i'au} (proposed meaning) - resets to level 0


This list is obviously in no way complete.

I think there should be some normalization of these both disparate proposal=
s and used constructs.
